00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.540
When creating Word documents, there will
be situations where you need to display

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.640
certain information in a table format.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.850
Word has tools within itself
to allow you to do this.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.890
And I'm going to demonstrate them here.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:16.650
The first way to insert a table is
to go to the insert tab, click on

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.990
that, and then select the table icon.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:25.320
And just below there, as I start
to move my mouse down the rows, and

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:30.540
then across, it automatically starts
to insert that amount of columns

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.220
and rows within to the letter.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.670
When I'm happy with the number of
columns and rows I want just click

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:37.200
and it will automatically insert them.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.130
The problem there is, is that I
still need to populate the table.

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:45.750
An alternative to this is importing
information from another document and

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.580
then converting that into a table.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.530
The first thing I'm
going to do is undo that.

00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.070
So that is now clear.

00:00:55.529 --> 00:00:58.269
I will then open the spreadsheet that
I downloaded from the vision2learn

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.169
website, which contains the
information that I'm going to use.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:05.220
So what I need to do is I need to
copy this information, so I'll click

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:09.780
and hold and drag it down and across,
and then select the copy icon.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.410
Now that I have copied that
information, I can then go back

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.490
to the letter and select paste.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.860
So as you can see it has now, pasted
the information into the letter.

00:01:20.775 --> 00:01:25.695
I now have several options so if I click
on the little drop on the paste options

00:01:25.695 --> 00:01:30.795
button, it gives me the option to keep
the source formatting, use the destination

00:01:30.795 --> 00:01:37.845
styles, link and keep source formatting,
link and use destination styles, insert

00:01:37.845 --> 00:01:39.785
as a picture or keep the text only.

00:01:40.325 --> 00:01:41.095
For this example.

00:01:41.095 --> 00:01:42.485
I'm going to keep the text only.

00:01:44.065 --> 00:01:47.175
So as you can see, it has now
inserted that text into the letter.

00:01:47.925 --> 00:01:50.835
But it isn't presented
in a very nice format.

00:01:51.645 --> 00:01:55.455
What I need to do now is I need
to convert that text into a table.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:02:02.375
To do that I need to highlight all of the
text and then go back to the insert tab.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:07.575
So I click on insert and go to table
and then select convert text to table.

00:02:08.805 --> 00:02:12.405
So Word is actually identifying
where the spacing is occurring

00:02:12.645 --> 00:02:14.415
within each of those pieces of text.

00:02:14.685 --> 00:02:17.235
And it's automatically identified
that it needs to have three

00:02:17.235 --> 00:02:18.445
columns and eight rows.

00:02:19.125 --> 00:02:20.845
It is separated by the tabs.

00:02:22.425 --> 00:02:26.535
So I click OK, that will
insert the text into a table.

00:02:28.215 --> 00:02:32.375
Once I have the information in the table,
I then want to apply some formatting.

00:02:33.465 --> 00:02:37.875
If I double click on the icon
at the top left of the table, it

00:02:37.875 --> 00:02:39.855
will open up the table design tab.

00:02:40.305 --> 00:02:45.345
From there I can apply table
styles, shading, border styles,

00:02:45.585 --> 00:02:47.055
variety of different things.

00:02:47.665 --> 00:02:50.865
In this example, all I'm going
to do is just to add some

00:02:50.865 --> 00:02:52.635
shading to the top border.

00:02:53.955 --> 00:02:57.705
Once that's done, and I'm
happy that it looks okay, I

00:02:57.705 --> 00:02:59.235
can then save if the document.

